id: pm-vcs-8xis
title: Design committed repository links local layers and typed obliteration
description: "Add native repository composition and lifecycle operations: committed links pin authorized repository and revision identities, local layers overlay an instance without changing commits, and authorized obliteration produces a typed payload state distinct from garbage collection, missing data or corruption."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-01T19:32:34.077Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T23:35:59.709Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 1800
acceptance_criteria: Committed links are reproducible and retain the linked repository authorization boundary; Local layers never alter commit identity and are visibly excluded from ordinary status; Obliteration is authorized audited and scoped by stable file identity; Checkout and verify distinguish obliterated content from missing and corrupt objects
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
risk: high
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T23:35:59.709Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — committed repository links are implemented as sparse linked instances (engine/instances.ts: instance link, shared object store, sparse views; test/instances.test.ts: 'a linked instance materializes its view, shares objects and keeps private state', 'concurrent instances share objects but never overwrite each other's state'). REMAINS — local layers that overlay an instance without changing commit identity are not implemented (grep for local-layer/overlay returns no matches). Typed obliteration is not implemented (grep for obliterate/Obliteration in engine/ returns no matches). Checkout and verify distinguishing obliterated content from missing and corrupt objects is not implemented. Two of four acceptance criteria are not met."
body: ""
